course: dictionary
lesson: 5854
title: Mallet: a tool, a sport stick and an instrument beater
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. A mallet is a hammer with a big, heavy head, but it is made to tap things without damaging them. Its head may be wood, rubber or plastic.
explain: «Croquet is a lawn game in which players hit wooden balls with long wooden mallets through small hoops pushed into the grass.» The clues are hit, balls, hoops and grass. So a mallet here must be a long-handled stick used to hit the ball. Check by swapping in your meaning: "players hit balls with long sticks through hoops" still makes sense.
explain: The topic around the word matters. In a music lesson, a mallet is a stick with a soft or hard head used to play a xylophone or drum. Ask yourself: what is being hit, and what is the word being used for?
fact: A mallet is a hammer with a big head made of wood, rubber or plastic.
fact: Mallets hit things without damaging them, so they can tap wood joints together or push tent pegs into the ground.
fact: Croquet is a lawn game where players hit wooden balls with long mallets; it became hugely popular in England in the 1860s.
fact: In music, a mallet is a stick used to play a xylophone or drum.
fact: Safety tip: hold the mallet firmly and keep your fingers clear.
exercise: «Players hit wooden balls with long wooden mallets through small hoops pushed into the grass.» What is a mallet in this sentence? | A tent peg | *A long-handled stick used to hit the ball | A bird with a long neck | A soft cloth for polishing
exercise: In design and technology, a teacher says a mallet is used to tap wood joints together. What is a mallet? | A flamingo's neck | A type of hedgehog | *A hammer with a big head, made to tap without damaging | A rubber glove
exercise: A xylophone player picks up a mallet. What is it? | A sharp knife | A hot drink | A long wooden hoop | *A stick with a soft or hard head used to play the xylophone
test: Why would a mallet be used to tap a wooden joint instead of a sharp tool? | Because it is only used in polo | *Because it hits without damaging the wood | Because it is always made of glass | Because it can play a tune
test: The word «mallet» has more than one meaning. Which two areas use mallets in these lessons? | *Sport and music | Cooking and swimming | Reading and writing | Cars and trains
exam: «Alice's flamingo keeps twisting round to look at her: it would be a useless croquet mallet.» Why would a real flamingo make a useless mallet? | It is made of wood | It lays eggs | It is too small to hold | *Its long neck is soft and bends, so it cannot hit the ball
